cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the ArcticQA dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "ArcticQA: a source-supported scientific question pipeline and abstention benchmark"
abstract: >-
  ArcticQA builds source-supported multiple-choice and short-answer questions
  from Arctic research papers, and measures how often a model abstains when no
  listed option is correct. The pipeline records every paid model call in a
  shared ledger, so each number in the paper has a receipt.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wilcox
    given-names: Ben
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenWilcox8/arctic-qa"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
keywords:
  - question answering
  - benchmark
  - abstention
  - Arctic science
  - large language models
